    <!-- Preconnect & Preload -->
    <link rel="preconnect" href="https://res.cloudinary.com" crossorigin>
    {#- The LCP preload. Two shapes, and the responsive one is OPT-IN
        (`preload_responsive_sizes`) so the eleven pages that do not opt in emit
        BYTE-IDENTICAL html -- hence the single-line if/else and the whitespace
        control on this comment, both of which are load-bearing.

        Default shape: a plain href. Those pages preload a CSS background (the
        .page-hero overlays); there is no <img> for the preload to agree with,
        so a responsive preload would describe a selection the browser never
        makes.

        Responsive shape: the target IS an <img> that cloudinaryResponsive
        rewrites, so the preload must carry the same candidate list the element
        will carry. Without it the preload picks one candidate by its href and
        the element picks another by its srcset, and the LCP photograph is
        downloaded TWICE (measured: preload w_1200, element w_800). The list
        comes from the transform's own generator, never hand-authored. #}
    {% if preload_image %}
    {% if preload_responsive_sizes %}<link rel="preload" as="image" href="{{ preload_image | cloudinaryDefaultSrc }}" imagesrcset="{{ preload_image | cloudinarySrcset }}" imagesizes="{{ preload_responsive_sizes }}">{% else %}<link rel="preload" as="image" href="{{ preload_image }}">{% endif %}
    {% endif %}

    <!-- Fonts: self-hosted, so no Google origins and no third-party round trip.
         The two Google preconnects and the Google CSS <link> are gone; the CSP
         lost both origins with them.

         Preload EXACTLY these two: the above-the-fold pair. The Cormorant
         italic and nothing else are deliberately not preloaded -- they are
         below the fold on every entry page, and preloading them would compete
         with the LCP hero image for bandwidth.

         Filenames are content-hashed, so `crossorigin` is required (fonts are
         always fetched in anonymous CORS mode; without it the preload is
         discarded and the file is fetched twice). -->
    <link rel="preload" href="/fonts/cormorant-garamond-var.16b298e9dcfa.woff2" as="font" type="font/woff2" crossorigin>
    <link rel="preload" href="/fonts/outfit-var.55112282293d.woff2" as="font" type="font/woff2" crossorigin>

    <!-- External Stylesheet -->
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="{{ '/styles.css' | assetUrl }}">

    <!-- Leaflet.js for Maps - lazy loaded when locations page is visited -->
</head>
